Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||09-20-2001||02:36 PM||||In the absense of AUS... I seem to recall him saying that the RH Drive steering column came from a Volvo- pretty much bolted right in.  As for the MC's... I don't know.  His GT was originally a Canadian production- he said the RH conversion was pretty rough when he first acquired the car- but AUS can do anything as we've all been witness to!||||reg||1
Z||000013||AusFiero||09-20-2001||03:24 PM||||This car unlike my GT is a cross shaft conversion. Everything is kept on the left and a series of strong shafts inside tubes runs under the dashboard to operate the clutch and brake. The acelerator is just a different cable. Yes the steeering rack used is Volvo 244 and is pretty much a bolt up to a Fiero. To answer another question MinnGreen Yes I will have a spare dashboard and RHD setup. My GT has everything on the right. Not always a good thing with Fieros as the heater box has to be moved. <BR>This SE is probably the car I will get but the t-topped four cylinder is getting mighty tempting just so I can own 2 t-topped cars. Well one is trashed but I think putting my V6 gear in will be easier than removing the t-tops from the GT. Any ideas on that. Anyone cut a set of t-tops off before?<P>God.... what am I doing on the forum at 5:18am. Must go back to bed now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
