Z||000026||AusFiero||09-24-2001||03:55 PM||||Yeah I would be willing to part with a RHD conversion Minngreen. I am not sure you would be willing to pay what they are worth though. In Australia I can get about $2000 (US$1000) for all the bits involved. Which isn't many. There is a lot of work involved though with moving all the bits to the right side. <P>The new car has a different kind of conversion done to it Boomtastic. It is a cross shaft conversion which leaves everything on the left hand side and operates them with a series of shafts in tubes running to the other side of the car under the dashboard. This I am a bit iffy about and am considering another car because of it. Please see <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010482.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010482.html</A>  and help me decide. <P>Jefrysuko the turn signal/parking lights get fitted to all local Fieros due to registration requirements. What they came out of I do not know. All I know is my GT had the same ones. They ae probably out of one of the many Japanese cars we have here.||||reg||1
